# Who has to review a change, for the branch ruleset's
# "require review from Code Owners" rule on main.
#
# The rule was switched on with no CODEOWNERS file in the repository, which
# means it had nothing to ask for: every pull request reported
# REVIEW_REQUIRED, and on a maintainer's own pull request nobody could satisfy
# it, because GitHub does not let you approve your own. The only way through
# was the organisation admin bypass, which is set to "always" — so the rule
# recorded an intention and enforced nothing.
#
# This file is what gives it something to enforce, and it matters now rather
# than earlier because the first outside contribution has arrived. An owner
# must have write access to the repository or GitHub ignores the line, which
# is why there is one name here and not two: SauravCodemotion is a maintainer
# for the purposes of CLA.md's allowlist, but is not a collaborator on this
# repository.
#
# What this does NOT change: a maintainer's own pull request still needs the
# admin bypass, because the ruleset asks for one approving review and you
# cannot be your own. Dependabot's pull requests can be approved normally —
# they are authored by the bot, not by you.

